hi so i'm shilotrata a second year  computational neuroscience phd student  at the donders institute in the  netherlands and today i want to talk to  you guys a little bit about truly  relaxing because i was replacing this  statistics professor the other week at  this beautiful place called corsendong  in belgium and whilst i was teaching  there i sat across from this  psychiatrist during dinner and he told  me that when he's really stressed he has  the tendency to just go home and binge  watch a lot of netflix series and eat a  lot of junk food and we kind of came on  the concept of truly relaxing versus  just coping with stress so today i want  to talk you through our conversation and  give you three things that i learned  about how to truly relax versus just  coping with stress so hopefully you  learned something and let's get straight  into it  so i think one of the first things you  have to do if you are struggling a  little bit with stress is to identify  what truly relaxes you so when i think  of truly relaxing for example i think of  buying books and reading books those are  two different hobbies by the way or i  think of really going back to my body  and like doing exercise for example  whereas when i think of coping with  stress it's more like sitting on the  couch and  binge watching netflix and i think  usually when we're at the point that  we're really stressed it's already a  little bit too late to truly identify  what relaxes us  so i would try to write down what  relaxes you before you are already at  the breaking point of stress because i  think at that point it's already a  little bit too late so if you have some  time right now just write down three  things that really relax you and you can  also put it down in the comments below  because i would love to read  how other people truly wind down so the  second thing is to do it when you are  not stressed yet so maybe you recognize  this that when you have a really busy  exam week and you're super stressed you  can think of a thousand things to do but  as soon as the exam is over you're kind  of left in this empty place of  what did i want to do with my life so i  think it's good to think about the  things that relax you when you are in a  very relaxed moment and one of the  things that i've really learned is when  you feel a stressful moment coming it's  kind of good to already imagine this  stressful moment and kind of work  yourself through it so imagine yourself  at that stressful presentation how you  will feel how your body will feel and  also what you will do after to calm down  because i think we can already mentally  prepare ourselves for quite stressful  moments if we go to this mental exercise  of seeing the stressful moment and also  seeing how you will cope with it and  then the last thing i want to give as  advice is to think of peak stress  moments and peak rest moments so i think  throughout the year we usually plan for  really stressful activities so we plan  all of those in but we don't really plan  in really truly restful weeks and i  think this is something i've learned  that it is really important so for  example i would try to every three  months three months for me works really  well but maybe you need it a little bit  more or a little bit less but every  three months to plan in a longer period  where you're truly resting and for me  that's like deconnecting from my work  deconnecting from the internet my  computer and usually going back into  nature with a couple of friends so i  love going to the forest for example or  rivers they are just environments that  truly inspire and relax me and i also  love being in bookstores all day and  like just reading different authors and  getting new information that's not  necessarily related to my field but i  try to in my year about every three  months to really plan in a longer period  so a week or at least a weekend to truly  let go of some of the stressors from  daily life and i would call this a  versus deep work i would kind of call it  deep rest so yeah these are just some  short tips that i learned on deep  breaths versus like a shallow rest i  would almost call it  let me know what you think and i'm  really curious about your experience and  how you truly deeply rest or get over a  stressful period so put it down in the  comments below  and otherwise see you next week bye
 

